mode: "100644"
text: "# The Sends Lever\n\nIf there's one Instagram-specific growth lever to obsess over in 2026, it's **sends** — DM shares.\nThis is Instagram's equivalent of TikTok rewatches or LinkedIn dwell time: the signal that\ndisproportionately drives reach to **new** people.\n\n> Re-verify the weighting periodically, but the principle — sends drive discovery — is well\n> established and confirmed by Instagram.\n\n## Why sends matter so much\n\nWhen someone **DMs your post to a friend**, Instagram treats it as the strongest possible quality\nendorsement — a person vouched for your content to someone they care about. So:\n\n- **Sends per reach are weighted ~3–5× higher than likes** for reaching non-followers.\n- It's the dominant signal on the **discovery** surfaces (Reels, Explore).\n- A useful benchmark: **~1–2% sends-per-reach is solid; ~3%+ can unlock much more non-follower\n  distribution.** (Track *sends per reach*, not raw send counts.)\n\nChasing likes is optimizing the weak signal. **Chase sends.**\n\n## What makes content send-worthy\n\nPeople send content for the same reasons they share anything (see `viral-reverse-engineering` for\nthe deeper psychology). The send-worthy buckets on Instagram:\n\n- **Relatable / \"this is so us\"** — content a person sends to a friend with \"this is literally you.\"\n  Recognition is the most reliable send trigger.\n- **Useful / reference** — a checklist, framework, or how-to worth sending to a colleague (\"you need\n  this\"). Doubles as a **save**.\n- **Conversation starter** — a take or question someone forwards to spark a chat (\"thoughts?\").\n- **Identity / values** — content that says what someone believes, sent to signal it.\n- **Genuinely funny / surprising** — sent for the reaction.\n\nBefore posting, ask: **who sends this, to whom, and why?** If there's no clear answer, it'll get\nviews (maybe) but won't *travel*.\n\n## Engineering sends into each format\n\n- **Reels** — the hook earns the watch; a relatable or useful payoff earns the send. End on a line\n  worth forwarding (\"send this to the founder who needs it\").\n- **Carousels** — reference value (frameworks, checklists) drives sends + saves. A strong, shareable\n  cover.\n- **A soft prompt** can help (\"share this with someone who…\") — but only when the content already\n  earns it; a prompt on weak content just looks needy.\n\n## The two gates around sends\n\nSends don't work alone:\n\n1. **Watch time / the hook (the gate before sends).** If the first ~3 seconds don't hold people, they\n   never reach the send-worthy payoff. A weak hook caps everything. (Route to `hook-writer` /\n   `reels-script`.)\n2. **Saves (the cousin of sends).** Save-worthy reference content (how-tos, frameworks) signals\n   return-value and often gets sent too. Package practical content as a **resource**, not a throwaway\n   tip.\n\n## Measure it honestly\n\nTrack **saves and shares** in **WoopSocial post analytics**, and **sends per reach** plus **watch\ntime** in **native Instagram Insights** (WoopSocial doesn't store those). Use it to learn *which*\ncontent people share, then make more of that. Don't\npresent any of this as data WoopSocial supplies.\n"
